Add an `ignore_fullscreen` window rule.

Mango already lets a rule drop client-driven maximize/minimize requests
(ignore_maximize, ignore_minimize), but xdg_toplevel.set_fullscreen is always
honoured, so a browser going fullscreen for a video drags the whole window into
the compositor's fullscreen state.

With ignore_fullscreen:1 the request is acknowledged instead of acted on: the
client is told it is fullscreen (so it renders fullscreen content) while the
window keeps whatever state the user put it in - fake fullscreen, on demand.
A window the user has really fullscreened stays fullscreen either way.

